        {
          "label": "b",
          "question_text": "Consider the non-right-angled triangle shown.\n\nThe area of a triangle (from Year 8) is $A = \\frac{1}{2}bh$\n\nWrite the equation for $\\sin C$\n\n$\\sin C = \\frac{h}{a}$\n\nMake $h$ the subject of the equation you wrote above.\n\n$h = a\\sin C$\n\nBy combining $A = \\frac{1}{2}bh$ and $h = a\\sin C$, derive the side-angle-side formula for triangle area.\n\n$A = \\frac{1}{2}b\\left( a\\sin C \\right)$",
          "answer": "$= \\frac{1}{2}ab\\sin C$",
